    "angle": 0,
    "content": "By Lemma 2.59, \\(\\mathcal{V}_n^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda} = (\\mathcal{V}^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda})_n'\\) in this case. By the compression theorem 2.53, since \\(n \\geq C\\), \\((\\mathcal{V}^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda})_n'\\) has a perfect ZPC strategy given that \\(\\mathcal{V}_{2^n}^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda}\\) has one. But \\(2^n \\geq N\\), and we already argued that these tailored games have perfect ZPC strategies. Hence, \\(\\mathcal{V}_n^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda}\\) has a perfect ZPC strategy when \\(n \\geq \\max(C, \\log N)\\). If \\(C \\geq \\log N\\), then we are done. Otherwise, we can iterate this argument and deduce the same for any \\(n \\geq \\max(C, \\log \\log N)\\). Since there exists some \\(t\\) for which \\(C \\geq \\underbrace{\\log \\ldots \\log N}_{t\\text{-times}}\\) we deduce that \\(\\mathfrak{G}_{\\mathcal{M}} = \\mathcal{V}_C^{\\mathcal{M},\\lambda}\\) has a perfect ZPC strategy. This proves (2) in Theorem 2.31.",
